.TH CP 1
.SH NAME
cp \- copy files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cp
.I from to
.br
.B cp
.IR file ...
.I dir
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cp
is a command built into the shell,
.BR sh (1).
It copies the file
.I from
to
.IR to ,
replacing what
.I to
held. When the last name is a directory, each
.I file
is copied into it under its own name. The copy gets the permissions of the
original (its owner is the one who copies).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if a file could not be copied.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mv (1),
.BR ln (1),
.BR sh (1)
.SH BUGS
Files only: no directories, no attributes
.RB ( tag (1))
copied.
